english_question:
In the figure, there is a gray sector OAB on a horizontal surface with an area of 30π \( \text{cm}^2 \), where the length of OA is 6 \( \text{cm} \) and OA is vertical to the ground. If the sector in figure (a) rolls to the right until point A touches the ground again, as shown in figure (b), how far does point O move ( ) \( \text{cm} \)?
A. 11π
B. 12π
C. 10π + 2\sqrt{3}
D. 11π + \sqrt{3}

As shown in the figure, the side length of the small squares on the grid paper is 1. The thick lines depict the three views of a certain tetrahedron. What is the surface area of this tetrahedron? ( )
A. 8 + 8 \sqrt{2} + 4 \sqrt{6}
B. 8 + 8 \sqrt{2} + 2 \sqrt{6}
C. 2 + 2 \sqrt{2} + \sqrt{6}
D. \frac{1}{2} + \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} + \frac{\sqrt{6}}{4}

Given the three views of a geometric body as shown in the figure, what is the volume of the geometric body?
A. 16 + \frac{4\pi}{3}
B. 16 + 32\pi
C. 32 + \frac{8\pi}{3}
D. 32 + 8\pi

In the figure, three squares with side lengths of 2 overlap. O1 and O2 are the centers of two of the squares. What is the area of the shaded region? ( )
A. 1
B. \sqrt{2}
C. 2
D. 2\sqrt{2}

In the figure, rectangle ABCD has E as the midpoint of side AB. Triangle ADE is flipped along line DE to form triangle A<sub>1</sub>DE. If M is the midpoint of segment A<sub>1</sub>C, then during the flipping process of triangle ADE, the following statements are correct: (Fill in the number) 
① MB ∥ plane A<sub>1</sub>DE; 
② |BM| is a constant value; 
③ A<sub>1</sub>C ⊥ DE.
